{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And if You deal thus with me.</b> If You, the perfect one, withhold the perfection of governance that is fitting from You, and govern them thus in a deficient manner — like the governance of a female — for my sake and for my honor, and do not associate others with me, so as not to impair my honor." "<b>Kill me, I pray, with killing, if I have found favor in Your eyes.</b> So that You will be able to appoint others through whom the governance of the people will be complete, as the Sages said (Shabbat 55b) of Samuel, that he died before his time so that the kingdom of the house of David might arise." "<b>And let me not see my wretchedness.</b> The wretchedness of the lack of governance caused on my account — for this will be harder for me than death."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:22.652093538Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}